textkit grep: no pattern
Options:
  --ignore-case    Match without regard to case
  --invert         Print the lines that do not match
  --count          Print only how many lines matched, per input
  --line-number    Put the line number before each line
  --only           Print each match on a line of its own
  --fixed          Take the pattern as text, not as a regular expression
  --group <int>    Print the text of this group of the first match, from 1
  --replace <str>  Print each matching line with every match replaced by this
  --flush          Write each line out as soon as it is found
  --buffer <int>   The read buffer, in bytes, which also bounds a line (default 16384)
Arguments:
  <args>...        The pattern, then the files to read; no file, or -, is standard input
